# Corresponding source

This image is built from public sources. Everything below is what went into
`update.img`, with the exact revision each part came from.

## Built from

| Part | Repository | Revision |
|---|---|---|
| MotionSense (the daemon, the agent, the board configuration) | https://github.com/zhu30844/MotionSense | `@APP_REV@` |
| SDK fork carrying the board configuration and the device tree | https://github.com/zhu30844/luckfox-pico-sdk | `@SDK_REV@` |
| Upstream SDK the fork is based on | https://github.com/LuckfoxTECH/luckfox-pico | see the fork's history |

The SDK fork carries MotionSense as a submodule at
`project/app/motionsense`, so the first repository is reachable from the
second at the revision this image was built with. The board configuration is
`@BOARD_CFG@`.

## Components under a licence that requires source

The image contains a Linux kernel (5.10.160), U-Boot, BusyBox and a Buildroot
userspace, all under the GPL or LGPL, and all built from the SDK fork above at
the revision named. That repository is public and will remain so; its
`sysdrv/source/` holds the kernel and U-Boot trees as shipped, and
`sysdrv/tools/board/buildroot/` holds the Buildroot configuration used.

The Buildroot package set is generated from
`project/app/motionsense/buildroot-packages.fragment` by
`project/app/motionsense/scripts/gen-buildroot-defconfig.sh`; the generated
defconfig is `sysdrv/tools/board/buildroot/motionsense_defconfig`.

## Rockchip media libraries

`librockit`, `librkaiq`, `librockchip_mpp` and `librga` are Rockchip's
prebuilt binaries, taken from the SDK's `media/` directory. Their terms travel
in the headers shipped beside them: `librockit` and the ISP headers carry
`GPL-2.0 WITH Linux-syscall-note OR Apache 2.0`, and the others reproduce the
Apache-2.0 notice in full. A copy of Apache-2.0 is in `licences/`.

These are Rockchip-internal builds rather than the public upstream ones — the
commit `media/mpp` records is not present in `rockchip-linux/mpp`, nor
`media/rga`'s in `airockchip/librga` — so the terms that apply are the ones in
the headers distributed with the binaries.

## Everything else

`THIRD-PARTY.md` inventories the rest, including the OSD sources (3-clause
BSD, text in `licences/`), the DejaVu font and Video.js.
